{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Its end</b> — after it is drunk, and after its drinking, like a snake it will bite you and sting you, in the sense of ישך (it stings). And from this matter פרש is called so on account of the פרישין that are on its legs."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:24.265020197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}